<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<Document xmlns="http://book.copticlingo.com/">
   <Role id="People">   
      <Group>
         <InsertDocument path="include/Ontos"/>
         
         <Season id="Other">
            <Section>           
               <Title>
                  <Language id="English">Response to the Catholic Epistle</Language>
                  <Language id="Coptic">A petj/k e~bol...</Language>
               </Title>   
               
               <Comment>
                  <Language id="English">         
                     The response to the Catholic Epistle is chanted. The response to the Catholic Epistle hymn is chanted before the reading of the Catholic Epistle:
                  </Language>
               </Comment>
               
               <Text>
                  <Language id="Coptic">
                     A petj/k e~bol n~je pic~mou tou logou pefiwt i~af[icarx hwc rwmi n~telioc 
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="English">
                     The Perfect One, Blessed of His Father, came and was incarnate as a complete man.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="Arabic">
                     الكامل بركة أبيه الكلمة أتى وتجسد كانسان كامل.
                  </Language>         
               </Text>
               
               <InsertDocument path="include/agpeya/DoxaPatriNoRole"/>
               
               <Text>
                  <Language id="Coptic">
                     A petqelqwlf nau e~rof. A petqelqwlf sop nemwten. A petqelqwlf asf hijen pic~tauroc. 
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="English">
                     They saw the slaughtered One. The slaughtered One is present among you. The slaughted One is crucified on the Cross.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="Arabic">
                     المذبوح نظروه المذبوح كائن معكم. المذبوح معلق علي الصليب.
                  </Language>         
               </Text>
               
               <InsertDocument path="include/agpeya/KeNinNoRole"/>
               
               <Text>
                  <Language id="Coptic">
                     Yai te ]no/~te. Yai te ]ceb/roc. }p~rockunic/c tw monw &lt;rictoc.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="English">
                     This is eloquent. This is miraculous. Woship is due to the only-begotten Christ.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="Arabic">
                     هذه العقلية، هذه الأعجوبة. السجود للمسيح الواحد.
                  </Language>         
               </Text>
               
               <Text>
                  <Language id="Coptic">
                     Ere pic~mou n~]t~riac eyouab. (2) Viwt nem Ps/ri nem Pip~neuma eyouab.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="English">
                     The blessings of the Holy Trinity: The Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="Arabic">
                     بركة الثالوث الأقدس، الآب والابن والروح القدس.
                  </Language>         
               </Text>
               
               <Text>
                  <Language id="Coptic">
                     Ere pic~mou n~]yeo~tokoc (2) Maria y~mau n~I/couc Pi,~rictoc.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="English">
                     The blessings of the Theotokos: Mary the Mother of Jesus Christ.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="Arabic">
                     بركة والدة الإله مريم أم يسوع المسيح.
                  </Language>         
               </Text>
               
               <Text>
                  <Language id="Coptic">
                     Ere pic~mou m~penpatriar,/c: (2) n~iwt ettai/out n~ar,ie~reuc papa abba (nim).
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="English">
                     The blessings of our Patriarch: The honorable father, Archbishop Pope (…).
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="Arabic">
                     بركة بطريركنا الأب المكرم رئيس الكهنة البابا أنبا (...)
                  </Language>         
               </Text>
               
               <Comment>
                  <Language id="English">         
                     In the presence of a metropolitan or a bishop:
                  </Language>
               </Comment>
               
               <Text>
                  <Language id="Coptic">
                     Ere pic~mou m~pene~pickopoc (m~penm/tropolit/c) (2) n~iwt ettai/out abba (nim).
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="English">
                     The blessing of our Bishop (Metropolitan), the honorable father Abba (…).
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="Arabic">
                     بركة أسقفنا (مطراننا) الأب المكرم أنبا (...)
                  </Language>         
               </Text>
               
               <Comment>
                  <Language id="English">         
                     Then the conclusion is chanted:
                  </Language>
               </Comment>
               
               <Text>
                  <Language id="Coptic">
                     Eue~i~ e~h~r/i e~jen pailaoc t/rf: je a~m/n ece~swpi. 
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="English">
                     Shall come upon this entire congregation, Amen. So be it.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="Arabic">
                     تكون مع جميع الشعب أمين. 
                  </Language>         
               </Text>
               
               <Text>
                  <Language id="Coptic">
                     Kayolikon: kayolikon.
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="English">
                     The Catholic Epistle…
                  </Language>
                  <Language id="Arabic">
                     الكاثوليكون.
                  </Language>         
               </Text>
            </Section>
         </Season>
      </Group>
   </Role>      
   
